message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that spins around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Container that gives perspective to the card */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  perspective: 800px;          /* Creates a 3‑D space */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

/* Back side – rotated 180° so it shows after flip */
.card .back {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  background: #f8f8f8;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3‑D perspective (`perspective: 800px`). |
| `.card` | The element that actually flips. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D space. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| `.front` & `.back` | Two faces of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the back face when it’s turned away from the viewer. The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it becomes visible after the flip. |

You can replace the text inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any other content you like. Adjust the `perspective`, `transition`, and `transform` values to tweak the speed, depth, and direction of the rotation. Enjoy!
